x86_64-windows  a class-typed throw is refused for this target: the Microsoft ThrowInfo chain has to be pointed at a class - a type descriptor and a catchable type per class, and a _CTA array listing the thrown class and its bases, which is how catch-by-base works on that ABI - and cxx1 emits the four objects for a fundamental type only. throw-class.notarget records the same lag. The header itself compiles for this target; it is throwing one of its classes that does not.
